# The Gradle wrapper's Windows batch script is CRLF by contract — `cmd.exe`
# mis-parses it otherwise — so it is pinned to CRLF on every platform and
# exempted from whitespace checking. Without the exemption `git diff --check`
# reads all 93 of its line endings as trailing whitespace and exits 2, which
# makes the same command disagree across machines and turns a delivery gate
# into a coin flip. Nothing else in the repository is touched: there is no
# blanket `text=auto`, so no other file's line endings are renormalised.
/gradlew.bat text eol=crlf -whitespace
